     <item>
      <widget class="QGroupBox" name="groupBox_3">
       <property name="title">
        <string>ArmorAddons</string>
       </property>
       <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout_2">
        <item>
         <widget class="DKFormListPane" name="armorAddons">
          <property name="whatsThis">
           <string>&lt;p&gt;The way a piece of armor looks when it's worn by an actor is determined by ArmorAddon forms, which specify the 3D models for worn armor. Each ArmorAddon is designed for a single race (and any races which use that one as their &quot;armor race&quot;) and a single body part or set of body parts. An armor can specify multiple ArmorAddons to support multiple races. One example from the base game is the Falmer Helmet, which has separate ArmorAddons for human and elf races, Khajiit, Argonians, and Falmer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An Armor form and an ArmorAddon form will both define a list of body parts. The list on the Armor form controls equipping and unequipping: which races are allowed to wear a given armor, and which armors can be worn concurrently. The list on the ArmorAddon form controls the visuals only, and uses a separate &quot;priority&quot; value to determine how to handle two overlapping ArmorAddons.&lt;/p&gt;</string>
          </property>
          <property name="showFormTypes">
           <bool>false</bool>
          </property>
          <property name="showMoveButtons">
           <bool>false</bool>
          </property>
          <property name="showRemoveButton">
           <bool>false</bool>
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </widget>
     </item>
    </layout>
   </item>
